1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,720
You pay every month.

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,751
And somehow, the debt barely moves.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,435
That's not because you're bad with money.

4
00:00:06,455 --> 00:00:08,277
Some debt is built to be slow.

5
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,792
Interest is added every month.

6
00:00:10,812 --> 00:00:12,378
If your payment barely covers it,

7
00:00:12,398 --> 00:00:13,918
you're running on the spot.

8
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:16,722
And here's the part nobody tells you.

9
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:19,635
The minimum payment is the most

10
00:00:19,655 --> 00:00:21,580
expensive button in your banking app.

11
00:00:22,367 --> 00:00:24,567
Here are six steps to get out faster.

12
00:00:24,587 --> 00:00:25,509
Let's begin.

13
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:26,863
One.

14
00:00:26,883 --> 00:00:28,314
Look at the whole monster.

15
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:30,778
Write down every debt:

16
00:00:30,798 --> 00:00:32,376
how much you owe, the interest rate,

17
00:00:32,396 --> 00:00:33,735
and the minimum payment.

18
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:35,642
Include everything:

19
00:00:35,662 --> 00:00:38,554
cards, store credit, buy now pay later, car loans,

20
00:00:38,574 --> 00:00:40,304
even money you owe friends.

21
00:00:41,067 --> 00:00:42,598
Most people have never seen

22
00:00:42,618 --> 00:00:43,622
the total in one place.

23
00:00:43,642 --> 00:00:45,342
It's scary for ten minutes.

24
00:00:45,362 --> 00:00:46,381
Then it's a plan.

25
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:47,697
Two.

26
00:00:47,717 --> 00:00:49,437
Escape the minimum payment.

27
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,074
Say you owe €3,000 on

28
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,739
a card at 20% a year.

29
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:55,523
Pay €60 a month,

30
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:57,478
and it takes about nine years.

31
00:00:57,498 --> 00:01:00,728
You pay around €3,500 in interest.

32
00:01:00,748 --> 00:01:02,206
More than the debt itself.

33
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,399
Minimums are often set as a

34
00:01:04,419 --> 00:01:05,943
small slice of what you owe.

35
00:01:05,963 --> 00:01:08,633
As the debt shrinks, the payment shrinks too,

36
00:01:08,653 --> 00:01:10,639
so the finish line keeps moving away.

37
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,020
Pay €150 a month instead, and you're free in about two years,

38
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,843
with around €680 of interest.

39
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:19,872
Same debt.

40
00:01:19,892 --> 00:01:20,725
Same rate.

41
00:01:20,745 --> 00:01:22,308
Seven years of your life back.

42
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:23,855
Three.

43
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:24,801
Pick an order.

44
00:01:25,567 --> 00:01:26,327
The avalanche:

45
00:01:26,347 --> 00:01:27,852
pay the minimum on everything,

46
00:01:27,872 --> 00:01:29,763
and throw every extra euro

47
00:01:29,783 --> 00:01:31,552
at the highest interest rate first.

48
00:01:31,572 --> 00:01:33,871
Mathematically, it saves the most.

49
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:34,991
The snowball:

50
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,667
smallest balance first.

51
00:01:36,687 --> 00:01:37,855
You close accounts quickly,

52
00:01:37,875 --> 00:01:39,587
and each win keeps you going.

53
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:43,727
In one study of about six thousand people in a debt programme,

54
00:01:43,747 --> 00:01:45,954
those who cleared small accounts first were

55
00:01:45,974 --> 00:01:48,050
more likely to clear all of their debt.

56
00:01:48,333 --> 00:01:50,613
So if the rates are similar, start small.

57
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:52,188
If one rate is much higher,

58
00:01:52,208 --> 00:01:53,414
kill that one first.

59
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:54,992
Four.

60
00:01:55,012 --> 00:01:56,376
One debt at a time.

61
00:01:57,333 --> 00:01:59,183
Spreading your extra money thinly

62
00:01:59,203 --> 00:02:00,748
across every debt feels fair.

63
00:02:00,768 --> 00:02:02,551
But then nothing seems to move.

64
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:08,773
Researchers found that people who focused their repayments on one account at a time felt more progress,

65
00:02:08,793 --> 00:02:10,283
and paid more aggressively.

66
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,177
So pay the minimum on all the others,

67
00:02:13,197 --> 00:02:14,930
and put every extra euro on one.

68
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:17,937
When it's gone, roll that payment into the next.

69
00:02:19,133 --> 00:02:19,393
Five.

70
00:02:19,413 --> 00:02:20,916
Make the interest smaller.

71
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:23,797
Call your bank and ask for a lower rate.

72
00:02:23,817 --> 00:02:25,460
It costs nothing to ask.

73
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:28,283
A cheaper consolidation loan can help too,

74
00:02:28,303 --> 00:02:30,798
but only if you stop using the old cards.

75
00:02:30,818 --> 00:02:32,442
Check every fee first.

76
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:34,858
Even a few points matter.

77
00:02:34,878 --> 00:02:39,111
On €3,000, going from 20% to 10% cuts the

78
00:02:39,131 --> 00:02:43,590
interest from about €600 a year to about €300.

79
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:44,897
Six.

80
00:02:44,917 --> 00:02:46,440
Don't refill the bucket.

81
00:02:47,367 --> 00:02:51,062
Keep a small emergency fund, even €500,

82
00:02:51,082 --> 00:02:52,192
so the next surprise doesn't

83
00:02:52,212 --> 00:02:53,997
go straight back on the card.

84
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:55,696
And when a debt is gone,

85
00:02:55,716 --> 00:02:57,423
send its old payment to the next one.

86
00:02:57,443 --> 00:02:59,106
Then, to your savings.

87
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:01,098
And keep it visible:

88
00:03:01,118 --> 00:03:02,280
a list on the fridge,

89
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,140
crossed out one line at a time.

90
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,479
Final message.

91
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,325
Debt isn't a character flaw.

92
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:10,378
It's a maths problem,

93
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:12,266
and maths problems can be solved.

94
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:13,311
List it.

95
00:03:13,331 --> 00:03:14,495
Pay more than the minimum.

96
00:03:14,515 --> 00:03:15,430
Pick an order.

97
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:16,219
One at a time.

98
00:03:16,239 --> 00:03:17,026
Lower the rate.

99
00:03:17,046 --> 00:03:17,958
Don't refill it.

100
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:21,432
This is education, not financial advice.

101
00:03:21,452 --> 00:03:22,981
If debt feels unmanageable,

102
00:03:23,001 --> 00:03:25,707
many countries have free debt advice services.

103
00:03:25,727 --> 00:03:27,562
If this helped, subscribe.

104
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:28,407
Next up:

105
00:03:28,427 --> 00:03:30,685
how to invest your first thousand euros.
